name: Diagram context keeps literal paths visible and planning separate
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dfd_literal_evidence.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: run threat-model:import {"path":"ctx.json","activate":true}
require-live-snap: 30 threat-model:import saved | imported
submit: map
require-live-snap: 25 SYSTEM SUMMARY | map
nav-mode:
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 Map ✓ | accepted
keys: Tab z Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 LINK DETAIL | focused-120x36
expect: " a\nb "
resize: 160x48
live-snap: focused-160x48
expect: " a\nb "
resize: 96x89
live-snap: focused-96x89
expect: " a\nb "
resize: 80x24
live-snap: focused-80x24
expect: " a\nb "
resize: 60x20
live-snap: focused-60x20
expect: " a\nb "
resize: 40x12
live-snap: focused-40x12
expect: " a\nb "
ask: Do all six sizes show the quoted literal path, including its edge spaces and escaped line break, while keeping the selected annotation and Back understandable?
keys: j
require-live-snap: 20 "a b" | next-source-40x12
keys: k
require-live-snap: 20 " a\nb " | original-source-40x12
resize: 120x36
keys: Enter s
require-live-snap: 20 PLAN A STUDY | separate-scan-draft
expect: 2 exact source paths
expect: " a\nb "
expect: No jobs started
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 s plan scan | original-topology
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 " a\nb " | original-context
ask: Does returning from the unsaved scan proposal restore the exact selected annotation without starting work or changing source membership?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dfd_literal_evidence.py @TMP_TARGET @ART inspect
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
